  "print": "pad",
  "_about": "AFRICAN BUSH ELEPHANT (sculpt overlay, 2026-11-05): a 3 m bull -- highest at the withers, the back dipping into a saddle and the rump sloping off; a deep barrel on pillar legs (the fore column folds at the wrist, the hind at a low forward knee), round fore feet with pale nails, oval hind ones; a big sloping head, Africa-shaped ears laid back over the shoulders, the trunk hanging almost to the ground (its own bone: it still swings), tusks curving out and up, the tail to the hocks with a black tuft. Skin wrinkled in rings on trunk and legs. (2026-11-08, fair_bases.py) The TUSKS' roots are FAIRED into the head (sharp.js horn `fair`): the smooth union of tusk and skin, a gum the body's colour, no crease. (2026-11-08, ears2.py) The EARS (ears2.py): one huge fan each (sharp.js `fin`), the outline in metres in the old ear's plane -- the long lobe below, the rounded back edge -- its front edge rooted down the side of the head and faired, held just clear of the neck and shoulder; cupped, its outer edge turned back, the rim blunt; the skin's colour, plain as the body's (no `bark` creases: they read as stripes), the hollow (toward the body) pinker.",
